# A hook that triggers itself must not take the server down.
#
# `deliver_effects` fires deferred triggers via `fire_hook_data`, which applies
# that hook's batch and re-enters `deliver_effects` — plain recursion on the
# engine's stack. Before MAX_TRIGGER_DEPTH this aborted the process with
# "fatal runtime error: stack overflow" (exit 134): a server kill reachable
# from two lines of softcode. The guide also claimed triggers could not recurse.
#
# Runs against the bare framework world; the looping object is built in-game.

> create
> tester
> secretpass
> secretpass
expect: Account created

> @eval local r = spawn({key="looper", kind="item", title="Looper"}) set_script(r, "function cmd_ping(this, actor, room, args)\n emit(actor, \"PING-START\")\n trigger(this, \"on_ping\")\nend\nfunction on_ping(this, actor, room, data)\n trigger(this, \"on_ping\")\nend") set_tag(r, "system:global") return "built"
expect: built

# The chain is cut at the depth limit instead of overflowing the stack.
> ping
expect: PING-START

# Still alive and dispatching afterwards — the real assertion.
> look
expect-not: Huh?
> say still here
expect: still here
